#
# zic(8) source for the TZif fixtures of tzif-zone-files.qtest; the zones are
# synthetic test zones, not extracts of the time zone database.
#
# The test compiles this file with the platform's zic at test time when zic
# supports "-b".  The fixtures in the "slim" and "fat" directories are the same
# zones compiled with zic 2022g (macOS) as follows:
#
#   zic -b slim -d slim tzif-zones.zi
#   zic -b fat -d fat tzif-zones.zi
#
# Qore/Dst: local mean time until 1990, then +02 with daylight saving time
# (+03) from the last Sunday in March to the last Sunday in October.  A slim
# file has the transitions up to the first daylight saving time change only;
# the TZ string in its footer ("TST-2TDT,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3") gives local time
# after that.  A fat file also has explicit transitions up to 2037.
#
# Qore/Wide: offset changes in 1850 and 2050, outside of the 32-bit range of
# TZif version 1 data (1901-12-13 to 2038-01-19); the footer is "<WT2>-2".

# Rule	NAME	FROM	TO	-	IN	ON	AT	SAVE	LETTER/S
Rule	Tst	1995	max	-	Mar	lastSun	2:00	1:00	D
Rule	Tst	1995	max	-	Oct	lastSun	3:00	0	S

# Zone	NAME		STDOFF	RULES	FORMAT	[UNTIL]
Zone	Qore/Dst	1:30	-	LMT	1990 Jan 1
			2:00	Tst	T%sT
Zone	Qore/Wide	0:20	-	LMT	1850 Jan 1
			1:00	-	WT1	2050 Jan 1
			2:00	-	WT2
